{% extends 'work-shop/_listing.html.twig' %}

{#
    Shared sponsoring page. Each period page extends this and provides:
      sponsoring_cadence       (string) - how it renews, e.g. "monthly", "every 6 months"
      sponsoring_other_periods (list)   - cross-links to the other periods: {label, href}
    plus the usual listing_* metadata from _listing.html.twig.
#}

{% block listing_body %}
    <p class="mb-4">
        Flow PHP is MIT licensed and always will be. Nobody pays to use it, and nobody ever has to.
        But keeping it that way is work that never shows up in a changelog: reviewing contributions,
        patching security issues, cutting releases, keeping the documentation honest, and paying for
        the infrastructure that builds and tests every commit.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-4">
        Sponsoring is the simplest way to help carry that. It is not a product with a feature list,
        it is a small recurring thank-you that buys maintainer time - and it comes with a place at
        the table.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">The Sponsor role on Discord</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
        Sponsors get the <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Sponsor</strong> role
        on the Flow PHP Discord server. It shows: your username gets its own color, so sponsors stand out
        in every conversation. And it opens the exclusive channels where the maintenance happens out loud:
        what is being worked on, what is being postponed and why, roadmap discussions before they become
        issues, and the honest trade-off conversations that never make it into release notes.
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-2">
        {% for feature in [
            'The Sponsor role, visible on the server',
            'A custom username color, so your name stands out',
            'Access to the exclusive sponsor-only channels',
            'Roadmap and design discussions before they land on GitHub',
            'A direct line to the maintainer, in a channel small enough to be read',
        ] %}
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1 inline-flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-orange-100/15 text-orange-300 dark:text-orange-100"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-3 w-3" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg></span>
                <span>{{ feature }}</span>
            </li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 mb-4">
        This is the first sponsor benefit, not the last. As sponsoring grows, so will what it includes -
        and existing sponsors get everything new at the price they signed up with.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">How the role reaches you</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
        The role is not sent automatically - there is one step you have to take yourself. Checkout is
        handled by Polar; afterwards you sign in to the
        <a href="https://polar.sh/flow-php/portal" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="underline underline-offset-2">Polar customer portal</a>
        with the email you bought with (no password - Polar emails a one-time code), open your order
        and connect your Discord account there. Nothing happens until you do. Once Discord is
        connected, Polar takes over: the server invitation and the granting of the Sponsor role are
        fully automated on their side - no screenshots to send, nobody to DM.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-4">
        The role is tied to the sponsorship: it stays granted while your sponsorship is active. When
        the sponsorship ends, the benefit expires with it and Polar's Discord integration takes the
        role away.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Renewal and cancelling</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
        This sponsorship renews automatically, {{ sponsoring_cadence }}. You can cancel anytime from
        the same customer portal: cancelling stops the next renewal, your sponsorship and the Discord
        role stay active until the end of the period you already paid for, and you can change your
        mind and un-cancel any time before that date.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">What it is not</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
        It is not a support contract. There is no SLA, no guaranteed response time, and no queue-jumping
        for issues - if you need the maintainer on your problem, that is what
        <a href="{{ path('work_shop_consulting') }}" class="underline underline-offset-2">consulting</a> is for.
        And it gates nothing: Flow PHP stays MIT and complete for everyone, sponsor or not.
    </p>
{% endblock %}

{% block listing_aside %}
    <p class="mt-5 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide muted">Other periods</p>
    {% for period in sponsoring_other_periods %}
        <a href="{{ period.href }}"
           class="group mt-2 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 px-3 py-2.5 text-sm no-underline transition-colors hover:border-slate-300 hover:bg-slate-50 hover:no-underline dark:border-white/10 dark:hover:border-white/20 dark:hover:bg-white/[0.05]">
            <span class="font-medium text-slate-900 transition-colors group-hover:text-orange-300 dark:text-white dark:group-hover:text-orange-100">{{ period.label }}</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="muted transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5">→</span>
        </a>
    {% endfor %}
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs muted leading-relaxed">
        Renews automatically, {{ sponsoring_cadence }}. Cancel anytime from the Polar customer portal -
        the role stays until the end of what you paid for.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs muted leading-relaxed">
        The role is not sent automatically. Use an email you can actually read at checkout - it is how
        you get into the customer portal, where you connect Discord yourself to claim the role. There
        is no password, Polar sends a one-time code to that address.
    </p>
{% endblock %}
